From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:22:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: take the controller IRQ trigger from the
 device tree

The controller interrupt is requested with IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING although the
X1E80100 device tree (and the other Qualcomm ones) declare it level high.
The request changes the mapping's type to edge, and it stays that way after
the driver unbinds. The next probe asks for the device tree's level type,
irq_create_fwspec_mapping() refuses ("type mismatch, failed to map
hwirq-203"), of_irq_get() returns 0 and the probe fails with -EINVAL, so the
sound card is gone until reboot.

On the Yoga Slim 7x this happens whenever the ADSP driver is reloaded, which
unbinds the LPASS SoundWire controllers, for example to boot the DSPs again
after resuming from hibernation. Leave the trigger type to the device tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 43591a18d..a3700de68 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1648,9 +1648,13 @@ static int qcom_swrm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ctrl->reg_read(ctrl, SWRM_COMP_HW_VERSION, &ctrl->version);
 
+	/*
+	 * Take the trigger type from the device tree. Forcing a rising edge
+	 * changes the mapping of a level interrupt, and the next probe after
+	 * an unbind then fails to map it ("type mismatch") and gets IRQ 0.
+	 */
 	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, ctrl->irq, NULL,
 					qcom_swrm_irq_handler,
-					IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING |
 					IRQF_ONESHOT,
 					"soundwire", ctrl);
 	if (ret) {
-- 
